+## Fit — the AI technician
+
+Fit is a small animated robot with a screwdriver that floats above the chat button on every page. Ask it
+anything about the business you are signed in to; it looks the answer up in TapTap, gives links, runs live
+tests on your MikroTik routers and prepares changes for you to approve. It runs on [Groq](https://console.groq.com).
+
+### Setup
+
+Add to `.env`, then rebuild and migrate (migration `0099_fit_ai`):
+
+```
+GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...
+# optional
+GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b            # main model (tool use)
+GROQ_FALLBACK_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile  # used when the main model is busy or retired
+FIT_TIMEOUT=45                            # seconds per Groq request
+```
+
+```bash
+docker compose up -d --build
+docker compose exec web python manage.py migrate
+```
+
+Without a key Fit still appears and shows what needs attention, and tells owners how to finish setup.
+
+**If Fit says it “could not reach its AI service”**, the owner sees the exact reason under the message. For a full
+step-by-step test (key loaded → DNS → HTTPS to api.groq.com → key accepted → model exists → tool calling works) run:
+
+```bash
+docker compose exec web python manage.py fit_check
+```
+
+It stops at the first broken step and says how to fix it. Common causes: `.env` changed without recreating the
+container (`docker compose up -d --force-recreate web`), outbound HTTPS blocked by a firewall, a model name Groq no
+longer offers (the check lists the ones it does), or Groq not accepting requests from the server's network (403).
+
+### What Fit can do
+
+* **Answer from your data** — vouchers (state, time left, devices, why one does not work, history), customer
+  reports, agents (sales vs the previous period, drops, money owed, collection rate), finance (revenue, profit,
+  margin, expenses, month target forecast), network status and a summary of what happened, top data users,
+  devices, team chat and help guides — always with links to the right page.
+* **Read live from MikroTik** — resources, sessions, interfaces, DHCP leases, IP bindings, neighbours, routes,
+  DNS, logs, queues, health; over TapTap Link (latest sync, optional fresh pull) or the API. Secrets are removed.
+* **Run tests with live traffic** — internet check, ping, traceroute, DNS, website and speed test, from the router.
+* **Notice things** — open customer reports, unreachable routers, sessions that should be offline, agent sales
+  drops and a month behind target appear in its speech bubble, with a badge and a blinking antenna.
+* **Take action — only when you approve** — freeze / unfreeze / warn / disable / enable a voucher, add or reduce
+  time, reset devices, block / unblock a device, disconnect a session, resolve a customer report, track a voucher,
+  send a chat message.
+
+### Safety
+
+* **One business only.** Every lookup starts from the business the signed-in person is working in
+  (`request.tt_business`). The model never gets a business parameter; vouchers, reports, routers and chats are
+  always looked up inside that business. Company A can never see company B.
+* **Role-aware.** Fit only gets the tools the person's role permits (a *View only* member cannot ask about finance
+  or routers), and only offers actions their role could do by hand.
+* **Two locks on every change.** Fit only *proposes*: a card appears with **Take action**. The change happens when
+  (1) the owner has allowed that group in Fit settings (gear icon in Fit; all groups start **off**) and
+  (2) the person pressing it has the permission. It is re-checked at that moment, must be used within 30 minutes,
+  can only be approved by the person it was offered to, and goes through the same code as the normal page —
+  so it appears in the voucher history and activity log with "approved in Fit".
+* **Prompt injection.** Customer messages, chat, device names and router comments are passed to the model as data
+  and it is told never to follow instructions found in them; even if it did, it can only propose.
+* **Customer reports.** With "Close fixed customer reports by itself" on, Fit resolves a report only when the
+  voucher was broken when reported and now works; everything else waits for a person.
+
+Code: `core/fit_ai.py` (Groq + loop), `core/fit_tools.py` (read tools), `core/fit_actions.py` (approved
+changes), `core/views_fit.py`, `core/models_fit.py`, `static/js/fit.js`, `static/css/fit.css`, tests in
+`core/test_fit.py`. Shortcut: press `/` then `f` on any page to open Fit.
